      "description": {
        "fun": "Burmy never goes out without its cloak. It wraps itself in leaves, sand or even household dust and rubbish, depending on where it last battled, and if the cloak gets damaged it patches it straight away with whatever is nearby. Like real bagworm moths, what happens next depends on its sex: females keep their cloak for life as Wormadam, while males grow wings and fly off as Mothim.",
        "guide": "Burmy is a Bug-type bagworm Pokémon that covers itself with a cloak of leaves (Plant Cloak), sand (Sandy Cloak) or refuse (Trash Cloak), depending on its surroundings. Females evolve into Wormadam and males into Mothim.",
        "tagline": "A bagworm that dresses in whatever it finds lying around.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Burmy (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Burmy_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
      "branches": {
        "text": "At level 20, a female Burmy becomes Wormadam and a male becomes Mothim. A female's cloak at that moment decides its Wormadam for good: Plant, Sandy or Trash Cloak, each with its own second type, while Mothim looks the same whichever cloak it wore. It mirrors real bag moths, whose females stay in their case while the males fly away.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Burmy (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Burmy_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
